    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In a Fibonacci series, each number is the sum of the previous two numbers. Also, the first two numbers are always 0 and 1."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The Fibonacci series containing the first six terms is given below:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "0, 1, 1, 2, 3, 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Mathematically,"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "Fibonacci(n) = Fibonacci(n - 1) + Fibonacci(n - 2)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Additionally, Fibonacci(0) = 0 and Fibonacci(1) = 1."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Let's see how we can calculate the 5th term of the Fibonacci series using different methods."
